        model_answer="Each extra lamp adds its resistance, so the total resistance of the series circuit increases and the current, I = V ÷ R, falls. The supply p.d. is also shared between more lamps, so each lamp has a smaller p.d. across it. With less current and less p.d., each lamp transfers less energy per second and is dimmer.",
