written("w13_claim_parallel_equal_share", 13, 5, "13d",
        stem="A student says: 'In a parallel circuit the current always divides equally between the branches.' Evaluate this claim.",
        points=[P("the claim is wrong: the current divides equally only if the branches have equal resistance", ["wrong", "incorrect", "not always", "only if", "equal resistance", "same resistance", "only when"]),
                P("each branch has the same p.d., so I = V ÷ R: the branch with the smaller resistance takes the larger current", ["same p.d.", "i = v", "v ÷ r", "v / r", "smaller resistance", "larger current", "inversely"]),
                P("e.g. with 6 Ω and 3 Ω branches the 3 Ω carries twice the current; the branch currents always add up to the total", ["twice", "example", "6 ω and 3 ω", "2 : 1", "add up to", "sum to the total"])],
        min_points=2,
        model_answer="The claim is wrong. The current divides equally only when the branches have equal resistance. Each branch has the same p.d. across it, so by I = V ÷ R the branch with the smaller resistance carries the larger current; for example with 6 Ω and 3 Ω branches the 3 Ω branch carries twice as much. Whatever the split, the branch currents add up to the current from the source.",
        hints=["What do the branches share: the current or the p.d.?",
               "Same p.d., different resistances: use I = V ÷ R for each branch.",
               "State whether the claim holds, explain the split, and give an example."],
        keywords="wrong unless equal R; same p.d., I = V/R; smaller R carries more",
        figure=lambda: sk.circuit(series=[("A", "A")], parallel=[[("R", "6 Ω")], [("R", "3 Ω")]], emf=""),
        sample_pass=["Wrong: the current only divides equally if the resistances are equal; with the same p.d. the smaller resistor takes more current, e.g. a 3 Ω branch takes twice the current of a 6 Ω branch",
                     "incorrect, because I = V/R with the same p.d. means the branch with less resistance carries the larger share"],
        sample_fail=["Correct, parallel branches always get the same current", "The current is used up in the first branch"])

